-- title:
--   K''-rationality of transported p^k-kernel polynomial coefficients
-- statement:
--   Fix $M'\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/\ell_g)$. Let $K''\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange` of the function field `xHFunctionField M' H` for $H=\ker((\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$. Let $p$ be prime, $p^k\mid M'$, and let $h\in \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)[X]$ satisfy: for every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f:L\to F'$ and every primitive $p^k$-th root of unity $\zeta'\in F'$, the coefficientwise image of $h$ under `coeffMap f` equals $\prod_{1\le a\le p^k/2,\ p\nmid a}\bigl(X-x(\zeta'^a)\bigr)$, where $x(c)$ is the first component of `toricPoint F' 1 c`, the standard Tate-curve $q$-expansion $c/(1-c)^2+\sum_{m\ge1}\bigl(\sum_{d\mid m}d(c^d+c^{-d})-2\sigma_1(m)\bigr)q^m$. Let $C$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, and form the `LevelPData` whose $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ are the coordinate pairs `tateToricPoint L 1` of the units $\zeta$ and $\zeta^2$. Assume that after applying $C$ (so $x\mapsto u^{-2}(x-r)$) both abscissae $x_P$ and $x_Q$ lie in $K''$. Then every coefficient of $\mathrm{C}(u^{-2d})\cdot h(\mathrm{C}(u^{2})X+\mathrm{C}(r))$, with $d=$ `gamma0PowDeg p k` $=\varphi(p^k)/2$ unless $p^k=2$ where $d=1$, lies in $K''$.
--
--   This is the rationality step asserting that the kernel polynomial cutting out the abscissae of the generators of $\mu_{p^k}$ on the Tate curve, once transported by the variable change that makes the $\ell_g$-torsion toric points rational, has all its coefficients in the modular function field $K''$ attached to level $M'$ and the kernel of reduction modulo $\ell_g$. It is used in the construction of a variable change producing étale Tate data with rational level structure, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_raw_etale_tate_weightOne_level_fst_level_snd_fst_of_ker`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_variableChange_raw_etale_tate_weightOne_level_fst_level_snd_fst_of_ker), and rests on the existence of modular forms on $\Gamma_H(M')$ whose $q$-expansion ratios realise these coefficients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_coeff_kernelVariableChangeDeg_mem_range_of_variableChange_tateToricPoint_one_fst_mem_range_of_ker.lean

